WEBVTT

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.960
Number One! That's Takeda's...

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:15.670
Don't tell me Toyotomi also got to Takeda...

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.170
Maybe they did.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:22.470
I doubt the old man Tiger of Kai
would get into it with us right now.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.270
At any rate, they're an opponent
we have to fight someday.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.060
Increase the speed!

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.430
We're going to smash through them!

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.310
Yeah!

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.190
Has old man Takeda fallen to Toyotomi?

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.080
I see.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.370
Of all my vassals,

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:47.620
Oyamada Nobushige showed
the greatest confidence in that lad.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:52.250
Hence, he did that lad's
bidding to the bitter end...

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:53.950
Yes.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.430
He met his end

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:59.380
in a way that showed Master Sanada
what it means to be a general.

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:01.760
Nobushige...

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:03.310
Young sir Oyamada

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:06.380
gave his life to leave
something behind for my master,

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:10.520
but whether it will serve to guide
my master in the next order he gives...

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:16.320
From what I saw...

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.860
He is at a critical juncture.

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:20.940
Since it has come to this,
I shall go to Satsuma.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.900
--I will serve by Master Sanada's side and--
--No need!

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.160
If you do this,

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:29.790
the sacrifice of Oyamada and
his men will truly have been in vain.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:33.920
But if things go wrong, this
will affect the future of Takeda...

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:37.340
We share the same fate.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.210
This is what it means to
truly raise another person

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.670
and entrust matters to the next generation.

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:46.010
This is a trial for me as well.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.930
Commander...

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:51.480
Become strong, Yukimura.

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.020
Do not lose sight of your path!

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.600
What of the movements of the
troops surrounding the village?

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:03.410
Sir, they have done nothing so far.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.360
They have shown no signs

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:07.790
of moving to harass our
people nor of attacking us.

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:11.990
They only seem to be keeping
an eye on the Takeda in force.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.210
I have arranged for us

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.830
to be informed immediately
should something happen.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.380
Having survived Toyotomi's
clandestine invasion of Oshu,

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:23.340
Date Masamune has taken back
control of the surrounding lands...

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:27.050
I expect he must be heading for Osaka...

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:29.980
I believe he should be passing nearby soon.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.770
But I am surprised.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.470
With his Right Eye taken,

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:36.650
I believe even the One-Eyed Dragon
may be in a precarious position now...

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:39.650
Mm, so that is what is going on.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:40.490
What?

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.400
That damn Toyotomi.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:58.460
All right! Here we go!

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:00.340
Yeah!

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:04.960
Commander, the men who were surrounding Kai

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:08.760
are posing as Takeda troops
and moving to intercept Date!

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.930
No sweat! Heads up!

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:12.810
Yeah!

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:55.070
Lord Masamune.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:04.120
I, Kojuro, have faith that you
are, without a doubt, still alive.

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:14.180
I cannot impress upon you
enough that you not act rashly...

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:16.550
I earnestly urge you...

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:27.230
Kojuro...

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:36.620
One-Eyed Dragon!

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:38.910
These guys aren't our troops!

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:42.080
It's a Toyotomi trap!

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:43.880
Had to be, right?

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:19.860
In the meantime,

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:24.420
having failed to stop Toyotomi
from subjugating Chosokabe,

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.000
Sanada Yukimura had just barely
managed to make his way to Kyushu.

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:30.800
And he was finally approaching
his destination of Satsuma.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:51.490
"As a man sows, so shall he reap " was well said.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:54.490
The turbulent times, this country,
making your way to Kyoto...

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.820
You are merely yet another
agent of carnage called a "general, "

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:01.120
who claims those things as his justification.

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:15.800
Why do you think young sir
Oyamada followed your orders, Master?

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:20.630
In times of peace, a man can be
shaped over time by his position.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:24.810
But right now, we live in turbulent
times and the future is uncertain.

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:27.860
If you try to learn to be a commander
after you're already in command,

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:30.030
it's too late.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:34.200
Young sir Oyamada gave
his life to show you that.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:38.860
In that moment,

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:41.910
having decided to aid Chosokabe,
what you should have done

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:46.540
wasn't to run to young sir
Oyamada's side when he was injured.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:48.840
You weren't even able to
carry through with your decision,

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:52.290
which you had made against our objections.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:55.050
If you're going to be like this forever,

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:58.800
even I'm going to have to start
thinking about serving elsewhere.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:12.020
I am so sorry! I am so sorry, Master Oyamada!

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:18.700
He would never have wanted you to apologize.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:23.620
What's important is what
you're going to do from here on out.

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:26.200
I have continued to wield
these spears in the hopes

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:28.960
that I might lay some small part of
the groundwork for clearing the way

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:31.210
for the future of the land of the rising sun.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:35.130
And yet, the world has remained ever the same.

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:37.930
What my spear-wielding has ultimately yielded

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:42.880
are nothing but the tears
and lamentations of many.

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:44.430
Upon this mission,

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:48.310
I have not even been able
to wield my spears decently.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:50.390
Not only that, but...

00:08:56.530 --> 00:08:58.320
My lord...

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:12.120
My lord...

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:15.420
Master Yukimura!

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:24.470
Could it be...

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:28.220
...that you are the gentlemen
defending this land of Satsuma?

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:32.350
We are envoys of Takeda,
come from the land of Kai.

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:37.900
I am called Sanada Genjiro Yukimura.

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:40.110
Where might I find your lead--

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.380
W-Wait!

00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:59.880
Please wait!

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:07.670
If you are members of
the force defending Satsuma,

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:10.180
by all means, I would like for you to hear me...

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:16.560
Did we get... Iured in here?

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:25.160
Hey, hey, hey! Did you get a look at that?!

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:28.860
My signature ambush tactic! Bait and ambush!

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:33.620
A-Are you the one leading these men?

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:37.460
Okay...

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:40.290
Beat them to a pulp!

00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:48.890
Please make sure you do not injure these people!

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:50.760
Yes, Sir!

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:58.280
I'm strong!

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:04.030
Your momma's bellybutton sticks out!

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:09.790
How unbridled and unpolished!

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:12.540
And yet, his next move is
hard to read because of it!

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:17.750
Are you copying my two-sword style?

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:21.420
Hurry up and get beat by me!

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:33.840
If you are the commander
of Satsuma's military force,

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:35.060
by all means, please hear me--

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:38.020
Shaddup! You retard!

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:41.440
If there is another
commander who is not you,

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:43.940
I beg of you to allow
me an audience with him!

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:46.990
Damn.

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:57.420
You're pretty good.

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:02.630
Ah! Then you will hear me out?

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:04.250
Then allow me to start over.

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:06.840
--I am...
--You let your guard down!

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:15.680
I'm the greatest! No one's a
match for Miyamoto Musashi!

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:18.390
Th-That was ungentlemanly...

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:21.850
You sure don't give up.

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:26.270
If you want to see him that badly,

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:28.980
I'll make a special exception
and let you see Gramps.

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:33.700
Follow me.

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:50.930
Is that man...

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:54.800
Gramps! They weren't Toyotomi's men!

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:58.730
We've got guests! They said
they're from the land of Ika!

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:02.430
N-Not Ika. We are from Kai.

00:13:02.530 --> 00:13:04.230
Who're you?

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:09.570
I am Sanada Genjiro Yukimura.

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:12.450
I am Takeda's vassal of the land of Kai.

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:15.120
I have come on behalf of my lord

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:17.820
to thwart Toyotomi's invasion here in Satsuma

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:20.200
and join your struggling force...

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:25.460
Hey, Gramps! Let me guess!
That's shochu wine, isn't it?!

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:27.920
It's water.

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:29.380
What a lie!

00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:33.010
You're not supposed to drink
that stuff until you're all healed up!

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:35.480
I told ya it's water!

00:13:37.150 --> 00:13:39.230
That ain't water!

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:43.850
That there's the best medicine of all.

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:47.570
Didja say yer name's Sanada Yukimura?

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:51.810
Envoy o' the Tiger o' Kai, eh?

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:54.370
You've gone to a lotta
trouble to come all this way.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:14:00.370
I'm Shimazu Yoshihiro of Satsuma.

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:02.250
Goodness!

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:08.500
Lord Shimazu Yoshihiro!
I did not know you lived!

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:16.260
Do you think it's about time
I could get an answer from you?

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:20.440
I haven't seen Lord Masamune's head yet.

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:22.930
Bring Toyotomi Hideyoshi here.

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:24.640
Or I can go see him.

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:30.600
If he really did defeat Lord Masamune,
then I've got a score to settle.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:34.860
It seems you have absolutely no
understanding of your situation.

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:38.410
The responsibility you bear
is grave, my dear Katakura.

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:40.780
As the man who thwarted us at Kawanakajima,

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:43.620
delaying the unification
of the land of the rising sun

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:46.250
as well as our expansion out into the world,

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:50.750
it is in part also your
obligation to work for Toyotomi.

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:52.380
You will be a staff officer

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:54.960
of the gigantic army that
will, in time, rule the world.

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:58.510
Don't you think it's a dream
come true for any man of war?

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:03.190
I've got no interest in any
world ruled by you people.

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:05.100
I'm sure you'll eventually change your mind

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:07.480
once Toyotomi takes the country.

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:11.360
After all, there will be no other
lord to serve except Hideyoshi.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:16.150
I just don't get it, Takenaka.

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:17.480
Get what?

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:19.990
Don't you think this a waste of time?

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:23.200
At the very least, you're not some idiot.

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:27.750
And yet, you take the last man in
the world who would listen to you

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:31.500
and try to recruit him using tactics
that have no hope of getting him to--

00:15:34.930 --> 00:15:38.090
I would ask you to watch what you say.

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:44.850
Understand that you have
no choice but to join our cause.

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:49.680
What are you in such a hurry for?

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:54.020
I'm sure you'll come to admire Hideyoshi, too.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:58.320
To admire his overwhelming strength.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:04.660
To think they'd set up a
fake force to egg me on...

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:07.960
Toyotomi uses some childish tricks.

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:11.760
Though, it looked as if
you had been fooled at first.

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:13.830
Did you perhaps hear the
Right Eye's voice remonstrating you

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:16.840
just as you were about to unsheathe that sword?

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:18.090
Damn.

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:20.550
This is likely an opening gambit.

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:23.880
Toyotomi probably intends to
decide on what measures to take next

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:26.260
depending on how we react.

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:30.190
If he went to the trouble
of throwing me against you...

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:32.810
It is unlikely that they
think such a tactic would result

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:36.190
in the Takeda and the Date's mutual demise.

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:40.620
They may be hoping that
we will join forces once again.

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:42.410
What do you mean?

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:45.610
They must want to dispose
of us both at the same time.

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:49.660
From their perspective, they boast
an overwhelmingly powerful force,

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:51.090
so rather than defeating individual opponents,

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:53.460
it is more convenient to
attack everyone at once.

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:56.010
Perhaps what is most desirable for Toyotomi

00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:59.800
is a reenactment of the
encirclement of the Oda.

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:04.470
All they do is sit back and wait.

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:06.550
Turn the tables on all their enemies at once

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:08.140
and bring the country under their rule, huh?

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:10.440
That's an awfully convenient scenario.

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:16.320
However, we could actually
take them up on it as well.

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:17.770
We may enter into an alliance,

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:21.980
but that does not mean we would
necessarily march on them together.

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:26.320
One-Eyed Dragon, what would
you think of trying to take Odawara?

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:30.210
If the Date take Odawara and we take Utsunomiya,

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:32.380
and we rely on Uesugi to play his part,

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:35.330
we would have warriors from
Kasugayama in Echigo to Oshu at our backs

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:39.920
and it would be possible for us
to form a solid wall across the east.

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:46.510
That may be a wise plan in its own way,

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:50.140
but you know what my answer is, right?

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:54.400
The Date Army will be
racing on straight for Osaka.

00:17:54.490 --> 00:17:58.230
There's something I've got to take back

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:02.490
and a score I've got to settle first.

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:04.280
If the Right Eye of the Dragon were here,

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:08.200
he might tell you to go along with my plan.

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:11.080
Too bad for you, Kojuro's not here.

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:13.160
That's why I'm going.

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:20.250
What's that Sanada Yukimura doing?

00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:22.430
I have sent him to Kyushu.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:26.850
To form an alliance with
the force defending Satsuma.

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:28.670
Well, bravo.

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:31.890
So you plan to attack from the far west as well.

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:33.850
But while I feel bad for him,

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:37.480
I'll be taking down
Toyotomi before that happens.

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:41.810
Surely, even you do not think
you can bring him down so easily.

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:44.740
No matter how much pride
and willpower you bring to bear,

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:47.200
they are not an opponent you
can win against in a proper fight

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:50.580
by charging into their inner
sanctum with a solitary force.

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:53.410
I don't plan to go there to die.

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:56.210
Not that there's any guarantee
that I won't die, either.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:19:00.880
A dragon who does not soar
may as well be dead to begin with.

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:03.080
Is that it?

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:04.970
That's right.

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:08.260
" I can't let him have it. "

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:09.640
When I saw those guys...

00:19:09.730 --> 00:19:15.520
When I first saw that bastard,
that was my gut feeling.

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:17.770
Toyotomi Hideyoshi...

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:22.150
True, he's strong, but there's
something that's not right.

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:25.480
I don't want to recognize his strength
as "strength, " even if it kills me.

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:29.320
There's something about him
that makes me feel that way.

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:35.580
Old man...

00:19:35.670 --> 00:19:40.660
If I end up kicking the bucket...

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:44.170
Nah, that's not me.

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:47.100
Give my best to Sanada Yukimura.

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:55.100
It seems Date hasn't been dissuaded
from marching his army on Osaka.

00:19:55.190 --> 00:19:59.180
Even after what he suffered at Suriagehara, too.

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:02.110
I've never seen an army that
was such an unknown quantity.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:06.610
Do you think the Tiger of Kai
proposed presenting a united front?

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:08.280
Of course.

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:13.610
Lord Shingen should be
well-acquainted with Date's disposition,

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:16.120
but finding himself face-to-face with Date,

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:20.040
he would still think of bringing
Date into his strategic plans.

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:23.210
As things stand, Takeda can't leave Kai.

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:27.010
Therefore, he'd try to get the
dear boy Masamune to take Odawara.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:30.430
The castle is more secure than it once was,

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:34.430
but he would judge that Date would
have a chance if he fought in earnest.

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:39.980
Rather than rushing us all at once
like when they were up against Oda,

00:20:40.070 --> 00:20:44.480
they would've tried to establish a
line of defense from Echigo to Odawara

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:48.860
to be in a position to wait for
the troops to come up from Kyushu.

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:53.160
That was what we actually wanted.

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:54.450
Primarily speaking,

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:56.620
the Toyotomi Army's forte is
not in defeating individual enemies,

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:59.040
but in sweeping through large-scale battles.

00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:02.090
They likely perceived that at Kawanakajima.

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:04.000
If we could turn that to our advantage

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:08.180
and make them think that we were
hoping they would conspire together,

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:11.100
I thought they would knowingly take us up on it.

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:13.390
After all, we arranged for
our new weapon to arrive

00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:16.430
right around when they would've
finished positioning themselves.

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:21.600
With your strength and that new weapon,

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:25.560
whether there was a line of
defense dividing the country in half

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:28.320
or whether we were attacked
from behind by a large force,

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:31.950
both our formation and strategy
would have remained fairly simple.

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:36.200
But thanks to the Date, I've been disappointed.

00:21:36.290 --> 00:21:39.660
Honestly, what a troublesome bunch.

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:43.210
But now, our course of action is set.

00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:45.790
Brilliantly done.

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:48.750
The country will finally
come under Toyotomi rule.

00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:50.430
Pardon!

00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:52.840
Lord Hideyoshi! Master Hanbei!

00:21:52.930 --> 00:21:54.300
What is it?

00:21:54.390 --> 00:21:57.930
A man claiming to be the head of the
Maeda family of Kaga is at our gates.

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:01.480
He is requesting an
audience with Lord Hideyoshi.

00:23:41.830 --> 00:23:44.570
The country seems to be in some kind of turmoil.

00:23:44.670 --> 00:23:46.880
What is this about a "next time "?

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:47.170
There is no guarantee that the
next day will dawn equally for all of us.

00:23:53.010 --> 00:23:55.880
You are quite the curious specimen.
